  "title": "Classification-Oriented Adaptive Sensing in Vision-Computer Networks",
  "summary": "Classification-oriented adaptive sensing leverages posterior sampling to enable high-performance, instance-adaptive compressed sensing through classification-driven extensions. This approach uses calibrated posterior uncertainty terms to guide sensing decisions, balancing measurement cost and classification accuracy.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "This work introduces a classification-driven extension of posterior sampling for adaptive sensing.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Calibrated posterior sampling helps estimate uncertainty and guide sensing directions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Experiments show that curtailment reduces posterior samples by up to 62% on MNIST with DDRM.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A sequential stopping rule optimizes measurement cost and classification accuracy.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
